# Secure dependency selection

Install packages in `admin/`. Root `package.json` only forwards scripts; do not `npm install` there.

```bash
# ❌ BAD — install at the repo root, or add a second UI kit
npm install some-ui-lib

# ✅ GOOD — from admin/
npm install <pkg>
npm audit
```

- Prefer the current stable release, not alpha/beta/nightly, unless the user asks.
- Prefer maintained packages. Skip ones with known high or critical vulnerabilities; pick a patched version or a safer alternative.
- Do not add a library the app already covers (UI follows `shadcn-only-ui`).
- The lockfile is `admin/package-lock.json`.
- After install, run `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint` in `admin/`, and say so if `npm audit` reports a new blocker.
